{"Using `pipeline.fetch_state(\"installation_id\")` as the default argument to `request.GET.get` causes it to be evaluated unconditionally, so if the pipeline state does not contain `installation_id` a KeyError will be raised even when the query string includes a valid `installation_id`, breaking the installation flow unnecessarily; should first read from `request.GET` and only call `pipeline.fetch_state` as a fallback when the parameter is missing": 0.8026787042617798}